---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Analytics privacy | ARISTURTLE" forceCompact>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[1000px] px-[5vw] pt-40 pb-24 text-white">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-12">Analytics privacy</h1>
    <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-300">
      <p>This page explains how ARISTURTLE uses optional website analytics. For questions about this use of your information, contact <a class="underline" href="mailto:info@aristurtle.gr">info@aristurtle.gr</a>.</p>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Your choice</h2>
        <p>Google Analytics loads only if you accept analytics. Rejecting it does not affect access to the website. You can accept or withdraw permission at any time using Analytics settings at the bottom of each page. Withdrawal stops future collection; it does not automatically delete information already collected.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">What analytics measures</h2>
        <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages people visit, where visits come from, and how visitors use our website. Depending on the enabled measurement features, this includes page views, approximate location, browser and device information, scrolls, and clicks on links to other websites. We use these reports to improve the site and understand interest in the team.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Google receives technical information needed to process those visits. Google states that GA4 does not log or store individual IP addresses. We do not enable Google signals or advertising personalization in the website integration.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Cookies and saved preferences</h2>
        <p>We remember your analytics choice in this browser's local storage for 180 days. If you accept, Google Analytics uses cookies such as _ga and _ga_* to distinguish browsers and sessions. Our integration sets their expiry to 180 days; continued consented visits may refresh that expiry. Clearing your browser storage removes the saved choice. Withdrawing permission also removes the default Google Analytics cookies set by this integration.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Google's processing</h2>
        <p>Google processes analytics data on its infrastructure, which may include processing outside your country. See <a class="underline" href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> and <a class="underline" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
